# SkinDx Bioc project rules

Before implementing a task, read the relevant project documents:
- `docs/PRD.md`
- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- `docs/DESIGN.md`
- `docs/SECURITY.md`
- `docs/DO_AND_DONT.md`
- `docs/API_CONTRACT.md`
- `docs/DATABASE.md`
- `docs/TESTING.md`

## Product boundaries
- `.in` is the ecommerce storefront.
- `.com` is primarily an informational and enquiry-focused site.
- Both use one shared Node.js + TypeScript backend and PostgreSQL database.
- One admin experience manages both sites with explicit role and site permissions.
- Do not assume site-specific content, prices, or visibility are shared unless the data model says so.

## Technical defaults
- Next.js App Router + TypeScript for frontends.
- Express + TypeScript for the API.
- PostgreSQL + Prisma for persistence.
- Zod for request and environment validation.
- shadcn/ui for UI primitives and Lucide React for icons.
- Axios must use a centralized, typed client per frontend.
- Cloudinary for managed media; Brevo for transactional email; Razorpay for `.in` payments; Google OAuth/OIDC for Google login.

## Non-negotiable security
- Never expose secrets to client code or commit real credentials.
- Enforce authentication, authorization, and site scope on the backend.
- Never trust client-supplied totals, roles, site access, or payment status.
- Verify Razorpay signatures and webhooks server-side; make webhook processing idempotent.
- Verify Google identity tokens server-side.
- Validate external input and upload restrictions.
- Do not invent medical/product claims, reviews, certifications, or compliance status.

## Implementation behavior
- Inspect existing files before editing; preserve established conventions unless they conflict with these rules.
- Prefer feature-based modules and small, cohesive changes.
- Do not add dependencies or empty abstractions without a reason.
- Do not implement a full feature when asked only to scaffold its structure.
- Add tests for security-sensitive behavior and changed business rules.
- Run relevant checks and report their actual outcomes; never claim unrun tests passed.
- If a requirement is ambiguous and materially affects security, money, data integrity, or regulated products, ask before guessing.


## Mandatory testing rule
- Every new API route must include relevant Jest tests in the same change; use Supertest for HTTP/API integration tests.
- Every new or changed Prisma model must include tests for its repository/service behavior and relevant database constraints/migrations. Do not pretend a model declaration alone needs a meaningless one-to-one unit test.
- Run relevant tests and report actual results. If tests cannot run, state why; never claim they passed.
- Never point tests at production. Use a dedicated disposable PostgreSQL test database and mock external providers for unit tests.
